# Commit and push after changes

When a requested change to this project is finished, commit it and push it without waiting for another confirmation.

- Commit only the files that belong to that change.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, keys). Warn instead of committing them.
- Do not commit `node_modules`.
- Do not update git config, skip hooks, or force-push.
- Use a short commit message that says why the change was made.
- Push the current branch to its remote after the commit succeeds.
- If Git is not installed, or the push fails, say so in the reply.
- If there is nothing new to commit, do not create an empty commit.
